<h2 data-i18n="guardTitle">Guardians of Light</h2>
</div>
<p class="section-intro" data-i18n="guardIntro">An ongoing conservation art project: endangered species portrayed through luminous threads, with a direct path from each artwork to the people working to protect the species.</p>
</div>
<div class="guardian-mission">
<div class="guardian-mission-copy">
<div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="guardMissionLabel">Project mission</div>
<p data-i18n="guardMissionText">Guardians of Light combines traditional drawing with digital illumination to make threatened species harder to overlook. The goal is a 20-piece series that connects visual attention with conservation awareness and support.</p>
<p class="guardian-method" data-i18n="guardMethod">Each portrait begins on 30 × 40 cm Clairefontaine Pastelmat with Faber-Castell Polychromos pencils, then receives its final light in Autodesk Sketchbook.</p>
</div>
