<div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="aboutTitle">About the Artist</div>
<p class="statement">Magyar Levente (Jalraxe) is a Hungarian visual artist combining traditional drawing with digital illumination to explore vulnerability, transformation and the fragile relationship between human attention and the natural world.</p>
<p class="about-copy">His drawings begin with the precision and physical presence of traditional media, then use restrained digital light as a narrative element rather than decoration.</p>
<p class="about-copy">His ongoing Guardians of Light series turns this visual language toward conservation, portraying critically endangered species as lives still visible—and therefore still possible to protect.</p>
